From: Erik Bitzek <e.bitzek@mpie.de>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 13:32:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Add fix mc/sites/kk: device<->host coherence around MC
 trial mechanics

Kokkos-aware subclass selected by -sf kk.  MC bookkeeping stays on the
host; the subclass implements the base-class hooks as
atomKK->sync(Host, ALL_MASK) / atomKK->modified(Host, ALL_MASK) so the
device rebuilds its atom set before each per-trial full-energy
evaluation (which runs through the Kokkos pair styles) and the host
sees current data after it.  Also register both /kk files in the
legacy-make Install.sh, conditional on their base-package files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0183gtTmwDnCVQWCaTxG4HPQ
